\DOC PROVE_SAFETY_SPEC_TAC

\TYPE {PROVE_SAFETY_SPEC_TAC : ?public_vars:term list -> thm * (thm option array) -> tactic}

\SYNOPSIS
Fully proves an existentially quantified constant-time/memory-safety
specification goal about an assembly routine, leaving no subgoals.

\DESCRIBE
Takes an optional {public_vars : term list}, the terms treated as the publicly
visible inputs on which the produced event trace may depend, and {exec : thm *
(thm option array)}, the execution record for the program: a theorem giving the
length of the byte list for the code paired with an array of
decoded-instruction theorems used to step through it. It applies to a goal
{
   ?- ?f. !x1 ... xn. t ==> ensures ...
}
\noindent (the implication's antecedent may be absent), where the postcondition
asserts that the newly appended event trace equals {f} applied to some of the
bound variables and satisfies a memory-access-inbounds condition. The tactic
discharges such a goal completely:
{
   ?- ?f. !x1 ... xn. t ==> ensures ...
   =================================================  PROVE_SAFETY_SPEC_TAC public_vars exec
}

\COMMENTS
All observed traces show this single outcome, on goals with no assumptions and
of this one shape: an existential witness for an event function over an
{ensures} specification with a {MAYCHANGE} frame.

\ENDDOC
